-- particles of one species are identical, so a state of several is defined only up to exchanging
-- them, and exchange acts on the state's sign: a fermion's flips it, a boson's leaves it. The sign
-- is a parity — cyc-sign's kind of datum, on particle labels rather than neighbours. Labelled points
-- keep the labels and drop this symmetry; this is what the classical picture compresses away first.
exchange-sign : Species → Bool → Bool
exchange-sign s b = if sp-fermion s then not b else b
